   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must provide customers clear safety notices promptly upon confirming a material safety risk, including the affected models and serial ranges, the nature of the risk, immediate precautions, and available remedies. A manufacturer must initiate a regulator-supervised recall of any model when its verified thermal-incident rate exceeds 8 incidents per 100,000 installed units for that model in a year. Rates must use documented incident and installed-unit data, with methodology and supporting data submitted to the regulator; customers must be notified promptly of the recall and provided repair, replacement, or refund instructions. A recall is also required when the regulator determines that a serious safety defect presents an unreasonable risk, regardless of the rate."
